<%# What just changed, for the dock's controller (it acts when the replaced
    element connects, and consumes data-changed so a Turbo Drive visit that
    reconnects the same node never acts twice). An inert <template>: it
    renders nothing. The dock renders it bare; Chats::Broadcasts sends it
    with the signal:

      data-changed               reload the recent list
      data-conversation-id       the conversation it was about, when the
                                 viewer can see it
      data-notify                a message they'd be notified about: its
                                 window may pop open, and it is announced
      data-sender-name           who it is from, for the announcement
      data-unread-count          unread there now, for the window's header

    Strings for people are rendered by the dock in the VIEWER's locale
    (Stimulus values), never here: a broadcast renders in no one's. %>
<% signal = local_assigns[:signal] %>
<%= tag.template id: "chats_dock_signal",
      data: {
        "chats--dock-target": "signal",
        changed: (true if signal),
        conversation_id: signal&.dig(:conversation_id),
        notify: (true if signal&.dig(:notify)),
        sender_name: signal&.dig(:sender_name),
        unread_count: signal&.dig(:unread_count)
      } %>
